WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.497 --> 00:00:16.681
"You've found Hosmer Angel?

2
00:00:16.941 --> 00:00:18.182
Where?" shouted Mr.

3
00:00:18.202 --> 00:00:21.563
Windibank, looking frantically around the room like an animal caught in a trap.

4
00:00:21.583 --> 00:00:23.544
"There's no escaping, Mr.

5
00:00:23.564 --> 00:00:25.145
Windibank," said Sherlock Holmes.

6
00:00:25.165 --> 00:00:27.746
"Sit down and let's talk this over."

7
00:00:28.606 --> 00:00:32.388
Our visitor collapsed in a chair with a ghastly look on his face and beads of sweat on

8
00:00:32.428 --> 00:00:32.808
his brow.

9
00:00:33.748 --> 00:00:34.749
"I've done nothing illegal!"

10
00:00:35.049 --> 00:00:35.869
he said defiantly.

11
00:00:35.889 --> 00:00:38.771
"That's right; nothing you did was illegal.

12
00:00:39.591 --> 00:00:42.173
But you played a heartless and selfish trick," said Holmes.

13
00:00:42.193 --> 00:00:46.315
"Now let me run through the series of events, and you can contradict me if I'm wrong."

14
00:00:47.136 --> 00:00:50.137
Mr. Windibank huddled in his chair like someone who was utterly crushed.

15
00:00:50.958 --> 00:00:52.799
Holmes sat down and rested his feet on the hearth.

16
00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:56.721
"A man married a much older woman for her money," began Holmes.

17
00:00:56.741 --> 00:01:02.412
"He also had the use of his stepdaughter's money for as long as she lived with them.

18
00:01:02.432 --> 00:01:06.235
The money was a considerable sum for people in their position, and the loss of it would have

19
00:01:06.255 --> 00:01:08.037
made a serious difference in their lifestyle."

20
00:01:08.857 --> 00:01:11.539
Mr. Windibank said nothing, so Holmes continued the story.

21
00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.262
The stepdaughter was a kind and friendly person.

22
00:01:15.102 --> 00:01:19.366
With her income and her outgoing personality, it was obvious that she would not remain single for long.

23
00:01:20.186 --> 00:01:24.390
Her stepfather needed to take action, so he kept her at home and prevented her from having any

24
00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:25.931
contact with people her own age.

25
00:01:26.832 --> 00:01:29.133
But he soon found that this would not solve the problem forever.

26
00:01:29.994 --> 00:01:32.156
The young woman became impatient and restless at home.

27
00:01:33.076 --> 00:01:37.000
She insisted upon her rights and finally announced that she would be attending the plumbers' ball with her

28
00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.563
mother. "What did her clever stepfather do then?"

29
00:01:40.943 --> 00:01:41.483
asked Holmes.

30
00:01:42.404 --> 00:01:46.047
"With the assistance of his wife, he disguised himself as Hosmer Angel.

31
00:01:46.908 --> 00:01:51.852
He covered his keen eyes with tinted glasses, masked his face with a mustache and bushy whiskers, and

32
00:01:51.892 --> 00:01:53.334
reduced his voice to a whisper."

33
00:01:53.354 --> 00:01:58.078
"And Miss Sutherland's poor eyesight made it even easier for the disguise to work," I said.

34
00:01:58.098 --> 00:02:00.440
"Exactly!" said Holmes.

35
00:02:01.376 --> 00:02:04.298
"The stepfather kept men away from her by pretending to court her himself."

36
00:02:04.318 --> 00:02:07.459
"It was only a joke at first," groaned Windibank.

37
00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.421
"We never thought that she'd fall for it so completely."

38
00:02:10.441 --> 00:02:12.862
"But she did," said Holmes.

39
00:02:13.843 --> 00:02:17.585
"She believed that her stepfather was in France, so there was no reason to suspect him.

40
00:02:18.506 --> 00:02:19.526
She was flattered by Mr.

41
00:02:19.586 --> 00:02:20.367
Angel's attentions.

42
00:02:21.988 --> 00:02:24.969
Her mother increased the effect by enthusiastically approving of Mr.

43
00:02:25.029 --> 00:02:28.251
Angel." Holmes said that after the ball it was essential for Mr.

44
00:02:28.311 --> 00:02:29.612
Angel to call on Miss Sutherland.

45
00:02:30.528 --> 00:02:33.850
It was obvious to her stepfather that the matter should be pushed as far as possible.

46
00:02:34.791 --> 00:02:37.913
An engagement would keep her—and her money—safe from any other men.

47
00:02:37.933 --> 00:02:41.516
"But the deception could not be maintained forever," said Holmes.

48
00:02:41.536 --> 00:02:44.518
"Those pretend journeys to France were rather awkward.

49
00:02:45.459 --> 00:02:49.241
It was clearly time to end the business in a dramatic way that would leave a huge impression

50
00:02:49.282 --> 00:02:49.862
on the young woman.

51
00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:53.805
She had to be prevented from thinking about other suitors for a long time."

52
00:02:54.725 --> 00:02:58.068
So on their wedding day, Hosmer Angel mentioned that something ominous might happen.

53
00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:02.783
And he made Miss Sutherland swear on a Bible that she would always be true to him.

54
00:03:02.803 --> 00:03:08.207
"You wanted Miss Sutherland to be tied to Hosmer Angel and so uncertain about his fate that she

55
00:03:08.247 --> 00:03:11.310
would not look at another man for many years," said Holmes.

56
00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:16.254
"So you conveniently disappeared by the old trick of stepping into one door of a carriage and out

57
00:03:16.274 --> 00:03:16.654
the other.

58
00:03:17.555 --> 00:03:18.876
I think that was the chain of events, Mr.

59
00:03:18.916 --> 00:03:20.938
Windibank! Don't you agree?"

60
00:03:21.798 --> 00:03:24.841
Our visitor had recovered some of his confidence while Holmes had been talking.

61
00:03:25.702 --> 00:03:28.204
Now he rose from his chair with a bitter sneer on his face.

62
00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.321
"It may be the chain of events, or it may not be, Mr.

63
00:03:31.361 --> 00:03:32.381
Holmes," he said.

64
00:03:32.401 --> 00:03:36.482
"But if you're so smart, you should be smart enough to know that you are the one breaking

65
00:03:36.502 --> 00:03:37.082
the law now.

66
00:03:38.022 --> 00:03:41.163
I have done nothing illegal from the beginning, but as long as you keep the door locked, I

67
00:03:41.183 --> 00:03:43.124
could sue you for assault and unlawful restraint."

68
00:03:43.144 --> 00:03:46.365
"As you say, the law cannot touch you."

69
00:03:47.245 --> 00:03:48.745
Holmes unlocked and threw open the door.

70
00:03:48.765 --> 00:03:51.726
"But there was never a man who deserved punishment more.

71
00:03:52.566 --> 00:03:55.587
If the young lady had a brother or a friend, he ought to horsewhip you."

72
00:03:56.467 --> 00:04:00.721
Mr. Windibank continued to sneer at Holmes, which brought a flush of anger to the detective's face.

73
00:04:00.741 --> 00:04:05.423
"It is not part of my duties to my client, but here's a riding crop, and I think

74
00:04:05.463 --> 00:04:06.183
I'll just use it."

75
00:04:07.144 --> 00:04:11.066
Holmes took two swift steps toward the whip, but before he could grasp it, Mr.

76
00:04:11.086 --> 00:04:12.426
Windibank dashed out of the room.

77
00:04:13.287 --> 00:04:16.008
With a loud clatter, he ran down the steps and out the front door.

78
00:04:16.908 --> 00:04:19.509
From the window we could see him running at top speed down the street.

79
00:04:19.529 --> 00:04:25.012
"He's a cold-blooded scoundrel," said Holmes, laughing as he threw himself down on his chair once more.

80
00:04:26.592 --> 00:04:30.755
"That fellow will get away with this act, but eventually he'll commit a crime so bad he'll wind

81
00:04:30.795 --> 00:04:31.536
up on the gallows.

82
00:04:32.417 --> 00:04:34.878
This case has had some interesting points to it after all."

83
00:04:34.898 --> 00:04:38.541
"I still can't follow all the steps in your reasoning," I said.

84
00:04:38.561 --> 00:04:40.683
"It was obvious that this Mr.

85
00:04:40.743 --> 00:04:44.546
Hosmer Angel must have had a strong motive for his strange behavior," said Holmes.

86
00:04:44.566 --> 00:04:49.569
"And it was equally clear that the only man who profited from the incident was the stepfather.

87
00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:52.732
The two men were never in the same place at the same time.

88
00:04:53.608 --> 00:04:56.470
In fact, Angel only appeared when Windibank was away."

89
00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:01.533
Holmes explained that the tinted glasses, whiskers, and strange voice all suggested a disguise.

90
00:05:02.513 --> 00:05:07.516
His suspicions were confirmed when Angel typed not only his letters to Miss Sutherland but also his signature.

91
00:05:07.536 --> 00:05:13.760
"This suggested that his handwriting was so familiar to Miss Sutherland that she would recognize even the smallest

92
00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:15.101
sample," said Holmes.

93
00:05:15.121 --> 00:05:18.503
"But how did you prove that Windibank and Angel were the same man?"

94
00:05:19.343 --> 00:05:19.924
I wanted to know.

95
00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:25.982
"Miss Sutherland had provided us with the name of her stepfather's employer—the wine importers Westhouse and Marbank of

96
00:05:26.042 --> 00:05:27.583
Fenchurch Street," said Holmes.

97
00:05:27.603 --> 00:05:31.644
"I wrote to Windibank at that address, asking him to come here.

98
00:05:32.525 --> 00:05:34.406
As I expected, his reply was typewritten.

99
00:05:35.286 --> 00:05:39.167
The individual letters looked exactly the same as those in Angel's notes to Miss Sutherland."

100
00:05:40.068 --> 00:05:42.109
Holmes took his investigation one step further.

101
00:05:42.989 --> 00:05:46.290
He started with the description of Hosmer Angel in Miss Sutherland's newspaper ad.

102
00:05:47.771 --> 00:05:52.093
Then he eliminated all the elements that could be a disguise—the glasses, whiskers, and voice.

103
00:05:53.013 --> 00:05:57.596
Finally he wrote a letter to the owners of Westhouse and Marbank, asking if they had any employees

104
00:05:57.656 --> 00:05:58.897
who matched that description.

105
00:05:58.917 --> 00:06:04.760
"In the same mail with Windibank's reply, I received a response from the wine importers," said Holmes.

106
00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:09.402
"They said that my description exactly matched one of their employees—Mr.

107
00:06:09.442 --> 00:06:10.303
James Windibank."

108
00:06:11.263 --> 00:06:13.785
The case was closed, but I had one more question.

109
00:06:13.805 --> 00:06:15.586
"What about Miss Sutherland?

110
00:06:16.346 --> 00:06:17.006
Will you tell her?"

111
00:06:17.326 --> 00:06:18.007
Holmes sighed.

112
00:06:18.027 --> 00:06:19.808
"She won't believe me, Watson.

113
00:06:20.756 --> 00:06:22.218
Miss Sutherland is in love with 'Mr.

114
00:06:22.278 --> 00:06:23.079
Hosmer Angel.'

115
00:06:23.941 --> 00:06:28.407
She would rather delude herself about him than accept the fact that he never actually existed."
